d from `collections.abc` inside the existing `TYPE_CHECKING` block next to `Any`.\n- The function builds `item_list = [str(item) for item in items]` once and formats only from that list. The output rules for lists are unchanged.\n- The docstring summary now reads \"Convert an iterable of items\", and the `Args` line is `items (Iterable): An iterable of items.`\n\nI did not run the wider test suite, the doctests, or the linters, since the spec only lists the one command. The test file was left untouched, as the spec requires.", "ttft_ms": 1558, "type": "result", "duration_ms": 14981, "uuid": "1b5fc6e3-c0b1-43c6-9c9a-d1b47db39d28", "ttft_stream_ms": 1352, "time_to_request_ms": 332, "first_content_frame_ms": 1352, "queued_turn_count": 0, "result_index": 0}
